<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nagapattinam</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Negapatnam, Negapatam</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nagapattinam is a port town on the coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tamil-nadu">Tamil Nadu</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, south of the Kaveri delta. Under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chola-empire">Cholas</a> it was a major harbour with a Buddhist monastery built with the support of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/srivijaya">Srivijaya</a> kings. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> took it from the Portuguese in 1658 and made it the capital of their <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coromandel-coast">Coromandel</a> possessions from 1690, until the British captured it in 1781.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nagapattinam.jpg" alt="Nagapattinam" width="320" height="400" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Aspandi007 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nagapattinam_Documentary.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
